   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "solution": "<p>False. The determinant of the coefficients is $\\begin{vmatrix}6&3\\\\4&2\\end{vmatrix}=6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=0,$ so by Cramer’s rule the system has no unique solution. In fact it has none: dividing the first equation by $3$ gives $2z_{1}+z_{2}=\\frac{8}{3},$ while dividing the second by $2$ gives $2z_{1}+z_{2}=2.$</p>",
